# Project groups for tabrail. Copy to groups.conf next to tabrail.tmux, or point the tmux option
# @tabrail_groups at a file of your own. A new tab joins the first group one of whose folders it was
# opened in or below; prefix M, a drag or the right-click menu moves it. Tabs in none: Default. The
# menu's "New group…" adds lines here; dragging a group's row in the sidebar reorders them. Columns:
# name (one word), tint behind the group's row (#rrggbb; a group menu's "Colour…" sets it to one of
# the palette file's), icon, folders (optional; a new tab of the group opens in the first).
# A line indented under another makes a subgroup, any depth deep: its parent is the nearest group line
# above it with less leading whitespace (a space or a tab counts one). The sidebar shows the tree, each
# level one column further right; folding a group hides its subgroups too.
Website   #283147  ◆  ~/src/website ~/src/website-staging
  Shop    #3a344e  ✦  ~/src/shop
Infra     #3b2f2a  ▲  ~/src/infra
Notes     #2a3b2f  ●
